{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויותירו", :translit "vayotiru", :gloss "and they left over"} {:he "ויותירו כדבר ה'", :translit "vayotiru kid'var Hashem", :gloss "and they left over according to the word of YHWH"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויותירו" "ויותירו כדבר ה'"]}], :frame {:text "The same verb describes two opposite outcomes: in Exodus 16:17 the Israelites leave over manna in obedience to Moses' instruction, and it is preserved; in Exodus 16:20 they leave it over in defiance of Moses' warning, and it rots. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the verbal identity as highlighting that the identical human act of leaving over produced blessing when aligned with divine command and curse when done against it.", :sources ["Exodus 16:17" "Exodus 16:20"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וירם", :translit "vayirem", :gloss "and it rose"} {:he "וירם כבוד ה'", :translit "vayarem kh'vod Hashem", :gloss "and the glory of YHWH was lifted up"} {:he "וירם לבם", :translit "vayirem libam", :gloss "and their heart was lifted up"} {:he "וירם כבוד ה' מעל הכרוב", :translit "vayarem kh'vod Hashem me'al ha-kheruv", :gloss "and the glory of YHWH was lifted up from upon the cherub"} {:he "ירום תולעים", :translit "yirem tola'im", :gloss "worms shall rise"} {:he "מאוד מאוד הוי שפל רוח שתקות אנוש רמה", :translit "me'od me'od havi shefal ruach she-tikvat enosh rimmah", :gloss "very very be lowly of spirit for the hope of man is maggots"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וירם" "וירם כבוד ה'" "וירם לבם"]} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay linking וירם (it bred worms / was lifted up) with ירום תולעים (worms shall rise)"}], :frame {:text "Sotah 5a states that anyone with arrogance of spirit is as though he pushes away the feet of the Shechinah, and that the glory of YHWH departs from him. The phrase 'worms shall rise' (ירום תולעים) is a wordplay on the identical root ר-ו-מ: the same verb that means 'it bred worms' (Exodus 16:20) can be read as 'worms 